<subpara id="X39400000QX016C_12" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___00002T200000">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>Read the freeze frame data using SST (TaSCAN). The freeze frame data records part of the engine operating condition when the malfunction occurred, and this information is useful when troubleshooting.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="X39400000QX016C_13" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="X39400000QX016C_13_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___00002T300000">
<scantool type="8"/>
<testtitle>Perform TaSCAN Active Test (VVT Control)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>With the engine stopped, turn the IG ON.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Following the SST (TaSCAN) screen display, select [Active Test] - [VVT Control].</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>With the engine idling, perform [ON/OFF].</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt/>
</specitem>
<table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
<tgroup cols="2" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
<colspec colnum="01" colname="C01" colwidth="2.01in"/>
<colspec colnum="02" colname="C02" colwidth="2.12in"/>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Performed (OCV operates)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Engine stalls or idles roughly</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry colname="C01" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Not performed (OCV does not operate)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry colname="C02" valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Normal idle speed</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="X39400000QX016C_13_0005" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="X39400000QX016C_13_0002" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="X39400000QX016C_13_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___00002T400000">
<testtitle>Inspect Camshaft Timing Oil Control Valve Assembly</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<test1>
<ptxt>Resistance Inspection</ptxt>
<test2>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance between the terminals.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Resistance</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.38in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.37in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1 - 2</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Approx. 20°C</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>6.9 to 7.9Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test2>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Operation Check</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A059895J04" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<test2>
<ptxt>Inspect the spool valve condition when battery voltage is applied between the terminals.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.14in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.42in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.57in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Specified Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1 - 2</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Battery voltage</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Valve operates</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Check that the spool valve is not stuck.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<ptxt>A spool valve that does not return properly due to foreign matter such as sludge being caught may cause a slight pressure leak to the advance side, which may cause a DTC to be detected.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</test2>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="X39400000QX016C_13_0004" fin="false">OK</down>
<right ref="X39400000QX016C_13_0006" fin="true">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="X39400000QX016C_13_0004" proc-id="RM0550J___00002T500000">
<testtitle>Inspect Wire Harness or Connector (Engine Control Computer - Camshaft Timing Oil Control Valve Assembly)</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>For the wire harness and connector inspection procedure and precautions, see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM0000005D701ZX"/>.</ptxt>
